      "summaryMarkdown": "Workspace, pins, lints, release profile, toolchain, alias and licences match WS-1/TGT-4, and `policy::tests` mutates the real manifests and fails on each drift (pins, local-path patch, lints, check-cfg, profile fields, members, edition, licence, components, dated channel, alias). Both target specs match TGT-1 (armv7: `llvm-floatabi = soft`, `+v7,+thumb2,+vfp3,+neon`, no `+soft-float`, vendor `tizen`, 32-bit), and `targets::tests` checks the fields and that the pinned nightly accepts both specs (`target_vendor=\"tizen\"`, neon/vfp3 cfgs). `cross` builds the right command line and environment for both targets: `-Zbuild-std=std,panic_abort -Zjson-target-spec --target <abs spec>`, `CC_`/`CFLAGS_` with clang `--target`/`--sysroot` plus the flutter-tizen armv7 flags, `CARGO_TARGET_<T>_LINKER=clang` with `-fuse-ld=lld -B<rustlib>/gcc-ld`, pinned `RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN`, `--clippy` with `-- ... -D warnings`, passthrough flags, `--all-tv-libs` from the workspace's cdylibs, and the early missing-rootstrap failure only for linking (cdylib, non-clippy) builds. I confirmed that the pinned cargo has `-Zjson-target-spec` and that the toolchain ships `llvm-ar`, `rust-lld` and `gcc-ld/ld.lld`. No `nsh-*` dependency. Two minor findings stay open: AGENTS.md documents commands that are not available yet, and inherited RUSTFLAGS silently drops the link args. One unverified risk for s3, not a finding: the x86_64 default rootstrap name `tizen-8.0-emulator.core` may be the 32-bit (i586) emulator rootstrap, with a separate 64-bit one; check it against the installed SDK at the first link.",
      "findingIds": [
        "s1-agents-doc-unavailable-commands",
        "s1-cross-rustflags-override"
      ],
