  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "s1-agents-doc-unavailable-commands",
      "boundaryId": "s1-workspace-gate",
      "criterionIds": [
        "WS-2"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "open",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected (WS-2):** `AGENTS.md`'s validation commands and cross-build text match the workspace, so an agent can run them.\n\n**Observed:** (1) `AGENTS.md` says cross builds go through `cargo xtask cross --target <armv7|x86_64|aarch64>` and names `TIZEN_ROOTSTRAP_AARCH64` (README.md repeats the variable), but `Target::parse` in `xtask/src/targets/mod.rs` rejects `aarch64` (`unknown target ... expected one of armv7, x86_64`); aarch64 is `d26-aarch64`, a later sprint. (2) The listed validation command `cargo xtask cross --target armv7 --release --check-symbols --all-tv-libs` can never succeed today: `run_cross` in `xtask/src/main.rs` (lines 92-96) runs the full release build and then fails with \"`--check-symbols` is not wired yet\".\n\n**Repair:** Document only what exists now: `--target <armv7|x86_64>` and the two rootstrap variables in `AGENTS.md` and `README.md`, adding aarch64 in the change that implements `d26-aarch64`. Either drop the `--check-symbols` validation line until `t2-symcheck` wires the checker, or mark it as arriving with `cargo xtask check-symbols`; preferably also make `--check-symbols` fail before Cargo runs (not after a full build) while it is unwired."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-cross-rustflags-override",
      "boundaryId": "s1-workspace-gate",
      "criterionIds": [
        "TGT-2"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "open",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected (TGT-2):** every `cargo xtask cross` build links with clang and `lld` against the rootstrap sysroot.\n\n**Observed:** `plan` in `xtask/src/cross/mod.rs` delivers the whole link configuration (`--target=<triple>`, `--sysroot`, `-fuse-ld=lld`, `-B<rustlib>/gcc-ld`, the armv7 flags) only through `CARGO_TARGET_<T>_RUSTFLAGS`, i.e. `target.<triple>.rustflags`. Cargo's flag sources are mutually exclusive in the order `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS`, `RUSTFLAGS`, `target.<triple>.rustflags`, `build.rustflags`, so when the caller's environment has `RUSTFLAGS` or `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS` set (common in CI: `actions-rust-lang/setup-rust-toolchain` sets `RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings` by default), all link args are silently dropped and clang links with its default linker and no sysroot. `execute` inherits the parent environment, and `Context` has no view of it, so `cross::tests` cannot catch this.\n\n**Repair:** Make the plan independent of inherited flags: pass the inherited `RUSTFLAGS`/`CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS` into `Context`, then emit one `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS` (unit-separator-joined) that merges them with the link args and clear `RUSTFLAGS`; or fail early with a clear message when they are set. Add a `cross::tests` case asserting the link args survive an inherited `RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings`."
    }
  ],
